":"/-5","page_id":"/","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/#internals","content":"Internals"},"8":{"id":"/-6","page_id":"/","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/#testing","content":"Testing"},"9":{"id":"/-7","page_id":"/","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/#what-booblik-is-not","content":"What booblik is not"},"10":{"id":"/-8","page_id":"/","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/#documentation","content":"Documentation"},"11":{"id":"/-9","page_id":"/","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/#license","content":"License"},"12":{"id":"/-10","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/","content":"A message broker in Kotlin/JVM built on an append-only log: a topic splits into partitions, a\npartition into segments, and a consumer reads by a numeric offset it keeps itself."},"13":{"id":"/-11","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/","content":"The niche is not \"a Kafka replacement\". It is a broker that fits in one head and one process — no\nZooKeeper, no KRaft quorum, no group coordinator. Everything that makes Kafka operable as a cluster\nis deliberately absent; everything that makes a log fast is reproduced and **measured**."},"14":{"id":"/-12","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#overview","content":"**Storage**: segments with a sparse offset index, two write paths (`FileChannel` and an FFM\nmemory mapping), rolling, recovery from a torn write, retention by size and by age"},"15":{"id":"/-13","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#overview","content":"**A per-partition writer actor** that groups whatever is already in its mailbox into one barrier —\nno timer, no configured window: the group size self-adjusts to the load"},"16":{"id":"/-14","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#overview","content":"**Its own network layer**: a selector loop, one coroutine per connection, a binary protocol, and\nFETCH served straight from the page cache to the socket with `transferTo`"},"17":{"id":"/-15","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#overview","content":"**Long FETCH** — a caught-up consumer waits on the broker instead of polling it, and a write\nduring the wait wakes it immediately"},"18":{"id":"/-16","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#overview","content":"**A client library**: a pipelined connection matched by correlation id, an accumulating producer,\na topic handle that routes by key, and subscriptions as `Flow<RecordBatch>`"},"19":{"id":"/-17","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#overview","content":"**A runnable broker**: configuration validated at startup, a metrics line, retention, a\ndistribution, and a container image with its own health check"},"20":{"id":"/-18","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#overview","content":"**Per-record CRC32C**, verified on every read that touches the bytes — which the zero-copy path,\nby construction, does not"},"21":{"id":"/-19","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#overview","content":"Topic creation is not coming: the set of partitions is fixed at startup on purpose. Neither are TLS\nand compression — both are incompatible with zero-copy by construction."},"22":{"id":"/-20","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#performance","content":"Measured on a rented Linux machine (ext4 on a local disk, nothing else running) and, for the\nend-to-end figures, on two such machines with a 7.85 Gbit/s link between them — the broker in its\nown process, the load generator on the other host.\ndocs/benchmarking.md has the methodology and the full tables."},"23":{"id":"/-21","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#performance","content":"PRODUCE ceiling, over the wire"},"24":{"id":"/-22","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#performance","content":"**1,404,750 records/s** (140,475 requests of 10 × 128 B)"},"25":{"id":"/-23","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#performance","content":"PRODUCE latency at 100k requests/s"},"26":{"id":"/-24","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#performance","content":"p50 **0.736 ms**"},"27":{"id":"/-25","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#performance","content":"FETCH"},"28":{"id":"/-26","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#performance","content":"wire-bound at 396.8 MiB/s — the link, not the broker"},"29":{"id":"/-27","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#performance","content":"Zero-copy versus a heap copy"},"30":{"id":"/-28","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#performance","content":"**2.5–2.8× less CPU per GiB served**, identical bytes"},"31":{"id":"/-29","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#performance","content":"Segment append, mapped, no flush"},"32":{"id":"/-30","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#performance","content":"11.1M records/s at 64 B — &#x2A;*13.9×** the `FileChannel` path"},"33":{"id":"/-31","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#performance","content":"Segment append, `fsync` per record"},"34":{"id":"/-32","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#performance","content":"2,769/s against 1,659/s — 1.7×"},"35":{"id":"/-33","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#performance","content":"Recovery"},"36":{"id":"/-34","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#performance","content":"**0.30 s per GiB** of log, which is why there is no separate index file"},"37":{"id":"/-35","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#performance","content":"Idle traffic of a caught-up consumer"},"38":{"id":"/-36","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#performance","content":"**0.50 requests/s** against 18.45 when polling"},"39":{"id":"/-37","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#performance","content":"Two of those rows exist because an earlier answer was wrong. \"Under durability the two write paths\nare indistinguishable\" and \"the mapped path has a worse worst second\" were both **properties of the\nstand**, not of the code: the first came from WSL2, where `msync` costs nothing next to the barrier,\nthe second from APFS, where the spread is 15.4× against ext4's 1.1×. Both are retracted in the\ndocument, next to the numbers that replaced them."},"40":{"id":"/-38","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#performance","content":"The harness itself cost more than most of what it measured. Running it inside the broker's JVM —\nwhich every end-to-end number before M-37 did — inflated the median by &#x2A;*9.2×** and cost 19 % of the\nceiling, because the two shared a heap, a scheduler and a GC."},"41":{"id":"/-39","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#runtime-footprint","content":"booblik targets a deliberately small JVM, and that is a constraint rather than a tuning knob — the\ntests and the benchmarks run under it too, so an allocation the hot path is not supposed to make\nfails the gate instead of production:"},"42":{"id":"/-40","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#runtime-footprint","content":"Measured cost: none worth mentioning — seven of eight benchmark rows match a default JVM within\nerror. Note that `-Xmx` does **not** bound a mapped segment: `FileChannel.map` is neither heap nor\ndirect-buffer memory."},"43":{"id":"/-41","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#runtime-footprint","content":"The broker prints these arguments at startup, and that is not decoration. The profile is baked into\nthe distribution's start script, and one `JAVA_OPTS` line in somebody else's `Dockerfile` silently\nreplaces it — after which what ships is a process nobody measured."},"44":{"id":"/-42","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#run-the-broker","content":"Or build it yourself — the script runs the gate, then `installDist`, then `docker build`, in that\norder, because the image has no build stage and a bare `docker build .` would package whatever\nhappens to be sitting in `booblik-app/build/install`:"},"45":{"id":"/-43","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#run-the-broker","content":"**62 MB to pull**, on `bellsoft/liberica-openjre-alpine:25` — Alpine with **glibc**, not musl, so\nthe runtime is the one the numbers above were measured on. Unpacked it is 240 MB as Linux docker\nreports it and 176 MB as Docker Desktop does, which is a fact about `docker images` rather than\nabout the image; the ratio is the portable part, and it is **half** of the same distribution on\n`eclipse-temurin:25-jre` (514 MB against 240 on the same host). Nothing is installed into the\nimage — busybox already covers what the start scripts call. Non-root under a pinned uid, data on a\nvolume, and a `HEALTHCHECK` that asks the broker METADATA rather than opening a TCP connection: the kernel accepts\na connection into the backlog with no help from the process, so a connect cannot tell a live broker\nfrom a hung one."},"46":{"id":"/-44","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#run-the-broker","content":"Without Docker:"},"47":{"id":"/-45","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#run-the-broker","content":"Configuration is `booblik.*` properties, and every one of them also reads from the environment with\nthe dots turned into underscores — `booblik.port` is `BOOBLIK_PORT`. An unknown key stops the broker\nat startup rather than surfacing at 3am."},"48":{"id":"/-46","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#use-the-client","content":"Snapshots only for now. The client pulls `booblik-core` and coroutines with it — the API hands out\n`Flow` and takes a `CoroutineScope`, so both are compile-scope dependencies rather than details\nbehind the module."},"49":{"id":"/-47","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#use-the-client","content":"Publishing, with the accumulator doing the work — the unit of a write is worth 54×, more than any\nother decision in this project:"},"50":{"id":"/-48","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#use-the-client","content":"Keys never reach the wire: the partition is chosen in the client, so the broker never has to agree\nwith it about hashing."},"51":{"id":"/-49","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#use-the-client","content":"Subscribing:"},"52":{"id":"/-50","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#use-the-client","content":"`follow()` waits and never completes; `replay()` ends at the high watermark as it was when the flow\nstarted. `StartPosition.Earliest` is the start of the **live** log, not zero — retention moves it."},"53":{"id":"/-51","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#use-the-client","content":"Back-pressure comes free: a slow collector suspends, and the fetch loop stops asking. That is the\nonly reason this is a `Flow` and not a callback. It hands over a **batch** rather than a record for\nan arithmetic reason — the `Flow` machinery costs 5.5 ns per emission and the `callbackFlow` channel\nanother 54, against 712 ns of end-to-end path per record; per batch of a hundred that is 0.008 %,\nper record it would have been 8 %."},"54":{"id":"/-52","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#use-the-client","content":"Positions are the consumer's own. `OffsetStore` is declared and deliberately not implemented, and\nthe word `commit` appears nowhere in its names, because the broker knows nothing about it."},"55":{"id":"/-53","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#internals","content":"Layer"},"56":{"id":"/-54","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#internals","content":"Segment"},"57":{"id":"/-55","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#internals","content":"`[int32 length][int32 crc32c][payload]`, body first and length prefix **last** — a crash between the two stores leaves a zero where recovery stops, not a plausible header in front of nothing"},"58":{"id":"/-56","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#internals","content":"Index"},"59":{"id":"/-57","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#internals","content":"sparse, one entry per N bytes, rebuilt from the segment at startup; a separate file would buy 0.30 s per GiB"},"60":{"id":"/-58","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#internals","content":"Writer"},"61":{"id":"/-59","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#internals","content":"one actor per partition, group commit, three ack policies (`NONE`, `WRITTEN`, `FORCED`)"},"62":{"id":"/-60","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#internals","content":"Transport"},"63":{"id":"/-61","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#internals","content":"own selector loop, or blocking sockets on virtual threads — both serve the same session code"},"64":{"id":"/-62","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#internals","content":"FETCH"},"65":{"id":"/-63","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#internals","content":"`transferTo` from the segment to the socket, or a heap copy; the slice is held across header **and** body so retention cannot move the log underneath a response"},"66":{"id":"/-64","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#internals","content":"Wire"},"67":{"id":"/-65","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#internals","content":"big-endian, `[int32 length][int16 apiKey][int16 apiVersion][int32 correlationId]`, versions per request rather than global"},"68":{"id":"/-66","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#internals","content":"Module"},"69":{"id":"/-67","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#internals","content":"`booblik-core`"},"70":{"id":"/-68","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#internals","content":"storage: segment, sparse index, two write paths, `transferTo`"},"71":{"id":"/-69","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#internals","content":"`booblik-client`"},"72":{"id":"/-70","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#internals","content":"the client **and the shared codec** — what a consumer of the library pulls in"},"73":{"id":"/-71","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#internals","content":"`booblik-net`"},"74":{"id":"/-72","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#internals","content":"the server: selector, sessions, two transports, two FETCH paths"},"75":{"id":"/-73","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#internals","content":"`booblik-app`"},"76":{"id":"/-74","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#internals","content":"running it: configuration, metrics, retention, distribution, health check"},"77":{"id":"/-75","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#internals","content":"`booblik-benchmark`"},"78":{"id":"/-76","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#internals","content":"the numbers: JMH through kotlinx-benchmark, plus the probes"},"79":{"id":"/-77","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#internals","content":"The codec lives with the client rather than with the server because it is **shared**: both sides\nhave to read the wire the same way, and a module both of them see is the only place a compiler\nchecks that."},"80":{"id":"/-78","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#testing","content":"104 tests across 23 classes, and the gate is one command:"},"81":{"id":"/-79","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#testing","content":"Some of them are worth naming, because they are what the ordinary ones do not cover:"},"82":{"id":"/-80","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#testing","content":"**Crash tests** kill a child JVM with `SIGKILL` mid-write, at varying moments, and demand that\nevery record the log admits to having is readable and matches its checksum — and that the next\nappend continues from the boundary recovery chose"},"83":{"id":"/-81","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#testing","content":"**Property tests** over random sequences of appends, rolls and truncations, with segments small\nenough that boundaries actually get hit"},"84":{"id":"/-82","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#testing","content":"**A no-locks gate** that reads the bytecode of the hot path and fails on `MONITORENTER`"},"85":{"id":"/-83","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#testing","content":"**A stress test** for the session loop, whose comment carries a warning: do not raise the round\ncount past the ephemeral port range, or the harness runs out of ports and blames the broker"},"86":{"id":"/-84","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#testing","content":"**`ci/smoke.sh`** starts the built distribution and speaks the protocol to it from Python that\nshares no code with the implementation — which is how it caught the record header growing from\nfour bytes to eight"},"87":{"id":"/-85","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#testing","content":"**`ci/docker-smoke.sh`** checks the image in a running container: the user, the six profile flags\nin the live process, configuration from the environment, the health check telling a live port from\na dead one, and that a pre-sized segment is still sparse on disk"},"88":{"id":"/-86","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#testing","content":"A milestone does not close without a measurement, and a measurement does not count if the stand is\nnot named. `MeasurementDir` refuses to run on tmpfs at all: `/tmp` is a RAM disk on most Linux\ndistributions, and a durability probe there reports `fsync` at 0.01 ms — a number that is not slow\nor fast but simply about something else."},"89":{"id":"/-87","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#what-booblik-is-not","content":"**Not a cluster.** One process, no replication, no leader election, no consumer groups. A broker\nthat dies takes its partitions with it until it comes back."},"90":{"id":"/-88","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#what-booblik-is-not","content":"**Not a Kafka client or server.** The wire protocol is its own, deliberately smaller, and it will\nnot talk to anything in the Kafka ecosystem."},"91":{"id":"/-89","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#what-booblik-is-not","content":"**Not configurable at runtime.** Topics and partition counts are fixed at startup; there is no\ncreate-topic request and no plan for one."},"92":{"id":"/-90","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#what-booblik-is-not","content":"**Not encrypted or compressed.** Both would mean touching the bytes on the read path, which is\nexactly what the zero-copy path exists not to do."},"93":{"id":"/-91","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#what-booblik-is-not","content":"**Not multiplatform.** The client is Kotlin/JVM. What is not portable in it is enumerable —\nsockets, `ByteBuffer`, two primitives from `java.util.concurrent` and `CRC32C` — and it now sits\nin one module, so the option is kept without paying for it today."},"94":{"id":"/-92","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#documentation","content":"docs/ — layered documentation: research, features with their BDD scenarios, the\nwire protocol, and a document per module. Written in Russian; code, KDoc and comments are in\nEnglish."},"95":{"id":"/-93","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#documentation","content":"Read research-architecture before changing anything. It\nseparates what was verified against a source from what was assumed, and it records the premises of\nthe original design draft that did not survive contact with the sources.\nBACKLOG.md holds the work items and, per milestone, what came out differently than\nplanned."},"96":{"id":"/-94","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#license","content":"MIT. See LICENSE."},"97":{"id":"/-95","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#license","content":"This build carries **13** hand-written documents and **42** generated pages."},"98":{"id":"/-96","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#license","content":"Generated pages carry a passport: which model wrote them, at which commit, from which files. Every citation into the code has been checked — the path exists, the lines are there, and the symbol named in the text appears within them."},"99":{"id":"/docs/README","page_id":"/docs/README","type":"page","content":"README","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/README"},"100":{"id":"/docs/README-0","page_id":"/docs/README","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/README#оговорка-про-статус","content":"Оговорка про статус"},"101":{"id":"/docs/README-1","page_id":"/docs/README","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/README#документы","content":"Документы"},"102":{"id":"/docs/README-2","page_id":"/docs/README","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/README#соглашения","content":"Соглашения"},"103":{"id":"/docs/README-3","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README","content":"`booblik` — брокер сообщений на Kotlin/JVM с хранением в append-only логе. Документация разложена\nпо слоям: от «почему архитектура именно такая» к «как это устроено на проводе» и «что внутри\nмодуля»."},"104":{"id":"/docs/README-4","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README","content":"Слой"},"105":{"id":"/docs/README-5","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README","content":"Папка"},"106":{"id":"/docs/README-6","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README","content":"Отвечает на вопрос"},"107":{"id":"/docs/README-7","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README","content":"Research"},"108":{"id":"/docs/README-8","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README","content":"`research/`"},"109":{"id":"/docs/README-9","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README","content":"почему архитектура именно такая; что проверено, что гипотеза"},"110":{"id":"/docs/README-10","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README","content":"Feature"},"111":{"id":"/docs/README-11","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README","content":"`features/`"},"112":{"id":"/docs/README-12","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README","content":"что делает система и зачем, BDD-сценарии = критерии приёмки"},"113":{"id":"/docs/README-13","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README","content":"API"},"114":{"id":"/docs/README-14","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README","content":"`api/`"},"115":{"id":"/docs/README-15","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README","content":"протокол на проводе"},"116":{"id":"/docs/README-16","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README","content":"Service"},"117":{"id":"/docs/README-17","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README","content":"`services/`"},"118":{"id":"/docs/README-18","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README","content":"зона ответственности модуля, конфиг, грабли"},"119":{"id":"/docs/README-19","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README","content":"Слоя `screens/` нет: клиента с интерфейсом у брокера не бывает."},"120":{"id":"/docs/README-20","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#оговорка-про-статус","content":"Инвариант: &#x2A;*`main` описывает то, что есть.**"},"121":{"id":"/docs/README-21","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#оговорка-про-статус","content":"Закрыты все вехи, **M0–M11**: хранилище, сеть, протокол и клиент, эксплуатация, проверки\nкорректности, подписки и долгий FETCH, поставка (образ в GHCR, клиент в reposilite), образец\nиз четырёх сервисов. Сегмент, разреженный индекс, две реализации записи, партиция с роллингом\nи retention, восстановление после рестарта, актор записи с батчами и групповым коммитом;\nсобственный acceptor на селекторе, бинарный протокол, FETCH мимо кучи; несколько топиков,\nконвейерное соединение, `Producer` с накоплением, `Consumer` со своей позицией и подписка как\n`Flow`; конфигурация с проверкой при старте, метрики, дистрибутив и образ со своей проверкой\nздоровья. 104 теста — оба пути записи и оба транспорта прогоняются через один набор утверждений."},"122":{"id":"/docs/README-22","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#оговорка-про-статус","content":"Потолок по проводу — **1,4 млн записей в секунду**, брокер отдельным процессом, генератор\nна другой машине (замер 16). Раннее число 267 тысяч снималось со стендом внутри JVM брокера\nи им же и было ограничено."},"123":{"id":"/docs/README-23","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#оговорка-про-статус","content":"Брокер запускается, обслуживает и переживает рестарт — это проверяет `ci/smoke.sh` в гейте."},"124":{"id":"/docs/README-24","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#оговорка-про-статус","content":"Чего не будет: создания топиков (набор партиций задаётся при старте), TLS и сжатия — они\nнесовместимы с zero-copy (§1.2), — и отставания потребителя в метриках: брокер не хранит позиции\nчитателей."},"125":{"id":"/docs/README-25","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#оговорка-про-статус","content":"Утверждения, которые по ходу работы **перестали быть верными**, — их стоит знать до чтения:\nбарьер через маппинг оказался не барьером (§1.9), индексный файл не нужен (§1.10), короткий\nзамер завышал маппинг в десять раз (§1.11), а zero-copy ничего не даёт ниже гигабайта в секунду\n(замер 7). Правьте по источнику, а не по памяти."},"126":{"id":"/docs/README-26","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#оговорка-про-статус","content":"Ресёрч отделяет **прогоны** (скомпилировано и запущено) от **чтения исходников** и от **гипотез**.\nПравите утверждение — перепроверяйте источник, а не соседний документ."},"127":{"id":"/docs/README-27","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#документы","content":"**Research**"},"128":{"id":"/docs/README-28","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#документы","content":"research-architecture — проверенные факты, решения, риски.\n&#x2A;*Точка входа для любого, кто берётся за задачу.** Две центральные посылки исходного драфта\nздесь опровергнуты по исходникам: Kafka пишет лог не через mmap (§1.1), а Ktor не отдаёт\n`SocketChannel` (§1.3)."},"129":{"id":"/docs/README-29","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#документы","content":"research-usecases — за чем к брокеру приходят и **что из этого\nстроится в booblik, а что рядом с ним**. Отвечает на вопрос про очередь задач: она не становится\nфичей брокера (Р11), а компактификация закрыта конструкцией — ключа нет на проводе (Р12)."},"130":{"id":"/docs/README-30","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#документы","content":"source-draft — исходный драфт задания, зафиксирован как есть.\nНе руководство к действию: расхождения разобраны в разделе 2 ресёрча."},"131":{"id":"/docs/README-31","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#документы","content":"**Образец**"},"132":{"id":"/docs/README-32","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#документы","content":"dev/ — четыре сервиса в `docker compose`, показывающие booblik в работе:\nраздача партиций и позиция у потребителя, очередь задач как протокол поверх лога, проекция\n(read model) и ретранслятор в Kafka и обратно. Собирается от **опубликованного** клиента\nи образа, поэтому ловит дефекты поставки, которых не видит сборка «всё вместе»: так нашлись\n`0.1.1` (корутины в `runtime`) и `0.1.2` (аккумулятор терял запись)."},"133":{"id":"/docs/README-33","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#документы","content":"**Совместимость клиентов**"},"134":{"id":"/docs/README-34","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#документы","content":"conformance/ — чем проверяется клиент на любом языке. Golden-вектора\nдля двух алгоритмов, которых **нет на проводе**, но которые обязаны совпадать: партиционер (ключ\nдо брокера не доходит) и CRC32C (на zero-copy-пути его проверяет только клиент). Плюс гарнесс\nиз 13 проверок против живого брокера — со своей реализацией протокола, потому что проверять\nпродюсера им же самим нечем. Контракт клиента и роли — там же; спецификация алгоритмов —\n§7 протокола."},"135":{"id":"/docs/README-35","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#документы","content":"**Клиенты**"},"136":{"id":"/docs/README-36","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#документы","content":"clients/ — паблишеры на Go, Python, Node.js и .NET (переписаны начисто,\nноль зависимостей) плюс Kotlin/Native — **таргет**, а не пятая реализация: он делит кодек с\nJVM-клиентом через `:booblik-protocol`. У каждого языка своя грабля в одной строке хеша, и это\nглавный аргумент за golden-вектора."},"137":{"id":"/docs/README-37","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#документы","content":"**Производительность**"},"138":{"id":"/docs/README-38","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#документы","content":"benchmarking — методика, профиль рантайма, правила и **все снятые числа**.\nВеха не закрывается без строки в этом документе."},"139":{"id":"/docs/README-39","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#документы","content":"**Features**"},"140":{"id":"/docs/README-40","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#документы","content":"feature-subscribe-and-publish — подписка на топик\nи публикация: `follow`/`replay`, долгий FETCH, хендл топика с маршрутизацией по ключу. Веха M7\nзакрыта, документ описывает существующее поведение."},"141":{"id":"/docs/README-41","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#документы","content":"feature-append-and-fetch — записать в лог и прочитать\nпо оффсету. Это весь брокер; всё остальное существует ради скорости этих двух операций."},"142":{"id":"/docs/README-42","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#документы","content":"**API**"},"143":{"id":"/docs/README-43","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#документы","content":"protocol-wire — бинарный протокол: кадр, PRODUCE, FETCH, коды ошибок."},"144":{"id":"/docs/README-44","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#документы","content":"**Services**"},"145":{"id":"/docs/README-45","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#документы","content":"booblik-core — хранение: сегмент, индекс, две записи, `transferTo`."},"146":{"id":"/docs/README-46","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#документы","content":"booblik-client — клиент и общий кодек."},"147":{"id":"/docs/README-47","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#документы","content":"booblik-net — провод: селектор, кодек, сессии, два транспорта."},"148":{"id":"/docs/README-48","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#документы","content":"booblik-app — запуск: конфигурация, метрики, retention, дистрибутив."},"149":{"id":"/docs/README-49","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#документы","content":"booblik-benchmark — числа: JMH и пробы."},"150":{"id":"/docs/README-50","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#документы","content":"**Бэклог** — ../BACKLOG.md, задачи `M-NN` по вехам M0…M11, все закрыты. Каждая\nвеха заканчивается строчкой итога: что вышло сверх плана и какая гипотеза не подтвердилась."},"151":{"id":"/docs/README-51","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#соглашения","content":"`id` во frontmatter = имя файла."},"152":{"id":"/docs/README-52","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#соглашения","content":"**Главный потребитель — Claude Code.** Каждый документ даёт якоря кода: путь к файлу, а не\nпересказ содержимого. Путь остаётся верным, копия протухает."},"153":{"id":"/docs/README-53","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#соглашения","content":"Один документ = одна сущность."},"154":{"id":"/docs/README-54","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#соглашения","content":"Числа в документах — только снятые прогоном, с указанием хоста и режима сброса. Без режима\nсброса число бессмысленно, а не неточно."},"155":{"id":"/docs/README-55","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#соглашения","content":"Гипотезы называются гипотезами; отклонения от драфта называются отклонениями."},"156":{"id":"/docs/README-56","page_id":"/docs/README","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/README#соглашения","content":"**Код по-английски, документация по-русски.** Идентификаторы, имена задач Gradle и сообщения\nоб ошибках — вербатим как в коде."},"157":{"id":"/docs/benchmarking","page_id":"/docs/benchmarking","type":"page","content":"Как здесь меряют и что намеряли","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/benchmarking"},"158":{"id":"/docs/benchmarking-0","page_id":"/docs/benchmarking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/benchmarking#как-запускать","content":"Как запускать"},"159":{"id":"/docs/benchmarking-1","page_id":"/docs/benchmarking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/benchmarking#профиль-рантайма","content":"Профиль рантайма"},"160":{"id":"/docs/benchmarking-2","page_id":"/docs/benchmarking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/benchmarking#правила-без-которых-число-ничего-не-значит","content":"Правила, без которых число ничего не значит"},"161":{"id":"/docs/benchmarking-3","page_id":"/docs/benchmarking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/benchmarking#замер-1-m0-2026-08-10-запись-в-сегмент","content":"Замер 1 (M0, 2026-08-10): запись в сегмент"},"162":{"id":"/docs/benchmarking-4","page_id":"/docs/benchmarking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/benchmarking#что-из-этого-следует","content":"Что из этого следует"},"163":{"id":"/docs/benchmarking-5","page_id":"/d