"/wiki/booblik-app-33","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfigtest","content":"Validation of configuration precedence and error handling. The test suite `BooblikConfigTest.kt:17-109` ensures that the configuration logic is robust. It specifically verifies that:"},"3115":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-34","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfigtest","content":"Defaults are applied when no configuration is provided `BooblikConfigTest.kt:34-41`."},"3116":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-35","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfigtest","content":"Environment variables take precedence over file settings `BooblikConfigTest.kt:44-50`."},"3117":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-36","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfigtest","content":"Invalid values (like non-integer ports) cause the application to fail fast rather than using silent defaults `BooblikConfigTest.kt:63-79`."},"3118":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-37","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#booblikconfigtest","content":"More: BooblikConfigTest"},"3119":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-38","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#main","content":"The broker lifecycle, including startup, metrics reporting, and shutdown hooks. The `main` function in `Main.kt:33-104` orchestrates the entire process. It initializes the `Broker` and `BooblikServer`, then launches two background coroutines for reporting metrics `Main.kt:85` and applying retention policies `Main.kt:86`. A `ShutdownHook` is registered to ensure the server and broker are closed in the correct order to prevent data loss `Main.kt:91-100`."},"3120":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-39","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#health","content":"The METADATA-based health check mechanism. The `Health` object in `Health.kt:32-86` provides a way to verify the broker is actually serving requests. Instead of a simple TCP connection, it performs a `sendMetadata` and `receiveMetadata` call `Health.kt:59-61`. This ensures the session loop and registry are functional. The check is designed to exit with code 0 if the broker responds correctly and code 1 if it fails or times out `Health.kt:70-83`."},"3121":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-40","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#application-distribution","content":"The build configuration and the health check start script. The `build.gradle.kts` file `build.gradle.kts:29-46` defines a custom task `healthStartScripts` to create a specific entry point for the health check. This script is included in the main distribution under the `bin` directory `build.gradle.kts:44`."},"3122":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-41","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"File"},"3123":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-42","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"Lines"},"3124":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-43","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"What is there"},"3125":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-44","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"`booblik-app/build.gradle.kts`"},"3126":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-45","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"`29-46`"},"3127":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-46","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"Registration of the `healthStartScripts` task and its inclusion in the distribution."},"3128":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-47","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"`…/app/BooblikConfig.kt`"},"3129":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-48","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"`49-55`"},"3130":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-49","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"The `init` block containing validation requirements for configuration."},"3131":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-50","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"`…/app/Health.kt`"},"3132":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-51","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"`59-62`"},"3133":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-52","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"The logic for sending and receiving metadata during a health check."},"3134":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-53","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"`…/app/Main.kt`"},"3135":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-54","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"`91-100`"},"3136":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-55","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"The shutdown hook implementation for graceful termination."},"3137":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-56","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"`…/app/BooblikConfigTest.kt`"},"3138":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-57","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"`63-79`"},"3139":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-58","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#key-files","content":"Test cases for ensuring invalid configuration values trigger errors."},"3140":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-59","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#behaviour-that-surprising","content":"`BooblikConfig.load` will throw an `IllegalStateException` if a configuration value is provided but is of the wrong type, rather than falling back to a default `BooblikConfigTest.kt:67`."},"3141":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-60","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#behaviour-that-surprising","content":"The `Health` check uses a separate thread with a `join` timeout to ensure that a hung broker does not cause the health check itself to hang indefinitely `Health.kt:66-73`."},"3142":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-app-61","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-app","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-app#behaviour-that-surprising","content":"The `Main.kt` shutdown hook closes the `server` before the `broker` to ensure that any in-flight batches are written to disk before the log is closed `Main.kt:94-98`."},"3143":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","type":"page","content":"booblik-benchmark","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","booblik-benchmark"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark"},"3144":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-0","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"What this module is responsible for"},"3145":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-1","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"3146":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-2","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#measurementdir","content":"MeasurementDir"},"3147":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-3","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#runtimefootprint","content":"RuntimeFootprint"},"3148":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-4","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#benchmarkconfiguration","content":"BenchmarkConfiguration"},"3149":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-5","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#flowoverheadbenchmark","content":"FlowOverheadBenchmark"},"3150":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-6","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#partitionwriterbenchmark","content":"PartitionWriterBenchmark"},"3151":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-7","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#groupcommitbenchmark","content":"GroupCommitBenchmark"},"3152":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-8","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#probes","content":"Probes"},"3153":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-9","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#key-files","content":"Key files"},"3154":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-10","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#behaviour-that-surprising","content":"Behaviour that surprising"},"3155":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-11","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `f508a4b65b3f`, 2026-08-15, sources: 6. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"3156":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-12","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"The `booblik-benchmark` module provides the infrastructure for measuring the performance and characteristics of the `booblik` system. It includes mechanisms to ensure measurement validity by enforcing physical storage usage and specific JVM configurations, a suite of JMH-based benchmarks for throughput and overhead analysis, and specialized \"probes\" for answering specific architectural questions."},"3157":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-13","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#measurementdir","content":"The mechanism for ensuring measurements are performed on physical storage rather than volatile filesystems like tmpfs. The `create` function in `MeasurementDir.kt:39-49` refuses to return a directory if it resides on a `tmpfs` or `ramfs` filesystem, preventing results that describe memory instead of disk."},"3158":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-14","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#measurementdir","content":"More: MeasurementDir"},"3159":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-15","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#runtimefootprint","content":"The verification mechanism that ensures the JVM is running with the specific memory and GC settings required for valid results. As implemented in `RuntimeFootprint.kt:24-46`, the module checks that required flags like `-Xmx64M` and `-XX:+UseSerialGC` are present in the runtime arguments."},"3160":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-16","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#benchmarkconfiguration","content":"The definition of different benchmark targets including `main`, `writer`, `flow`, `decode`, `ci`, and `quick`, as well as the `common` throughput settings. The configuration is defined in `build.gradle.kts:57-125` and uses a `common` function to set `mode = \"thrpt\"` and `outputTimeUnit = \"s\"` as seen in `build.gradle.kts:157-162`."},"3161":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-17","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#flowoverheadbenchmark","content":"A benchmark measuring the cost of the `Flow` abstraction by comparing `loop`, `coldFlow`, and `bufferedFlow` with varying `batchSize`. This benchmark is implemented in `FlowOverheadBenchmark.kt:40-86` and uses a `@Param` for `batchSize` to observe how the cost per emission changes."},"3162":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-18","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#partitionwriterbenchmark","content":"Measuring the cost of the write actor and batching by varying `batchSize`, `mode`, and `ackPolicy`. The benchmark in `PartitionWriterBenchmark.kt:45-90` uses `@OperationsPerInvocation(RECORDS_PER_OP)` to ensure the score is reported in records per second."},"3163":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-19","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#groupcommitbenchmark","content":"Evaluating the throughput of durable writes as the number of `producers` increases, considering `groupWindowMillis` and `mode`. This is handled in `GroupCommitBenchmark.kt:45-99`, where the score is measured in invocations per second."},"3164":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-20","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#probes","content":"A collection of standalone `JavaExec` tasks designed to answer specific questions about system behavior (e.g., `probeDurability`, `probeStartup`). These are registered in `build.gradle.kts:132-154` and map task names to specific probe classes."},"3165":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-21","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#key-files","content":"File"},"3166":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-22","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#key-files","content":"Lines"},"3167":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-23","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#key-files","content":"What is there"},"3168":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-24","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#key-files","content":"`…/benchmark/MeasurementDir.kt`"},"3169":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-25","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#key-files","content":"`32`"},"3170":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-26","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#key-files","content":"The `VOLATILE` set containing `tmpfs` and `ramfs`."},"3171":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-27","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#key-files","content":"`booblik-benchmark/build.gradle.kts`"},"3172":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-28","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#key-files","content":"`157-162`"},"3173":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-29","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#key-files","content":"The `common` configuration function for benchmarks."},"3174":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-30","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#key-files","content":"`…/benchmark/FlowOverheadBenchmark.kt`"},"3175":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-31","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#key-files","content":"`44-45`"},"3176":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-32","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#key-files","content":"The `batchSize` parameter definition."},"3177":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-33","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#key-files","content":"`…/benchmark/GroupCommitBenchmark.kt`"},"3178":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-34","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#key-files","content":"`49-61`"},"3179":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-35","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#key-files","content":"Parameters for `producers`, `groupWindowMillis`, and `mode`."},"3180":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-36","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#key-files","content":"`…/benchmark/PartitionWriterBenchmark.kt`"},"3181":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-37","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#key-files","content":"`48-55`"},"3182":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-38","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#key-files","content":"Parameters for `batchSize`, `mode`, and `ackPolicy`."},"3183":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-39","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#key-files","content":"`…/benchmark/RuntimeFootprint.kt`"},"3184":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-40","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#key-files","content":"`24`"},"3185":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-41","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#key-files","content":"The `REQUIRED` list of JVM flags."},"3186":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-42","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#behaviour-that-surprising","content":"The `MeasurementDir.create` function will throw an `IllegalStateException` if the directory is on a volatile filesystem, as seen in `MeasurementDir.kt:43-47`."},"3187":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-43","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#behaviour-that-surprising","content":"In `GroupCommitBenchmark.kt:42-43`, the score is reported as **invocations per second**, meaning the user must multiply by the number of producers to get records per second."},"3188":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark-44","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark#behaviour-that-surprising","content":"The `PartitionWriterBenchmark.kt:98-101` includes `log.retainAtMost` inside the measured `append` method to ensure retention costs are included in the benchmark."},"3189":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","type":"page","content":"MeasurementDir","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","booblik-benchmark"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir"},"3190":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir-0","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"3191":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir-1","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"What this module is responsible for"},"3192":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir-2","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir#measurementdir","content":"MeasurementDir"},"3193":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir-3","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir#volatile-filesystem-refusal","content":"Volatile Filesystem Refusal"},"3194":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir-4","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir#the-create-lifecycle","content":"The `create` Lifecycle"},"3195":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir-5","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir#filesystem-description","content":"Filesystem Description"},"3196":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir-6","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir#key-files","content":"Key files"},"3197":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir-7","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"Behaviour that surprises"},"3198":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir-8","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `f508a4b65b3f`, 2026-08-15, sources: 6. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"3199":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir-9","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","content":"Documentation for the `MeasurementDir` component within the `booblik-benchmark` module, focusing on its role in ensuring measurement integrity by preventing volatile filesystems and providing environmental context."},"3200":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir-10","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"The `MeasurementDir` object is responsible for ensuring that any directory used for benchmarking is backed by physical storage rather than volatile memory. It prevents the \"false speed\" trap where `fsync` operations return instantly because they are only hitting RAM, as seen in the failure where a probe reported 0.01 ms `fsync` on `tmpfs` (`MeasurementDir.kt:10-13`)."},"3201":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir-11","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir#measurementdir","content":"The core object responsible for creating valid measurement environments. It acts as a guard against invalid measurement mediums, ensuring that the results reflect disk performance rather than memory speed (`MeasurementDir.kt:27-49`)."},"3202":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir-12","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir#volatile-filesystem-refusal","content":"The mechanism that prevents measurements on `tmpfs` or `ramfs` to avoid measuring memory instead of disk. The module defines a set of `VOLATILE` filesystems (`tmpfs`, `ramfs`) (`MeasurementDir.kt:32`) and will refuse to return a directory if the `FileStore` type matches these, as a measurement on such a medium is considered \"fiction\" (`MeasurementDir.kt:33-47`)."},"3203":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir-13","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir#the-create-lifecycle","content":"The process of resolving the base directory via `booblik.bench.dir` and validating the `FileStore` type. The `create` function first checks for the `booblik.bench.dir` system property (`MeasurementDir.kt:40`); if absent, it defaults to `build/measurements` (`MeasurementDir.kt:40`). After creating the base directories (`MeasurementDir.kt:41`), it validates the `FileStore` to ensure the medium is not volatile before returning a new temporary directory with the provided prefix (`MeasurementDir.kt:41-49`)."},"3204":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir-14","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir#filesystem-description","content":"The `describe` function and its role in providing the medium's identity in report headers. This function attempts to retrieve the `FileStore` for a given path to return a string containing the filesystem type and name (`MeasurementDir.kt:58-62`), which is used in probe reports to ensure results are comparable across different hosts (`MeasurementDir.kt:54-56`)."},"3205":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir-15","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir#key-files","content":"File"},"3206":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir-16","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir#key-files","content":"Lines"},"3207":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir-17","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir#key-files","content":"What is there"},"3208":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir-18","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir#key-files","content":"`…/benchmark/MeasurementDir.kt`"},"3209":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir-19","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir#key-files","content":"`27-49`"},"3210":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir-20","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir#key-files","content":"The `MeasurementDir` object containing logic for directory creation and validation."},"3211":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir-21","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir#key-files","content":"`…/benchmark/MeasurementDir.kt`"},"3212":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir-22","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir#key-files","content":"`58-62`"},"3213":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir-23","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir#key-files","content":"The `describe` function for filesystem identification."},"3214":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir-24","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"The `create` function will throw an `IllegalStateException` rather than issuing a warning if a volatile filesystem is detected, because a warning is often ignored after the number has already been believed (`MeasurementDir.kt:24-25`)."},"3215":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir-25","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-benchmark/measurementdir#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"The default measurement directory is not the system's temporary directory (`java.io.tmpdir`), but `build/measurements`, to ensure measurements land on a real filesystem where the source tree lives (`MeasurementDir.kt:22-23`)."},"3216":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","type":"page","content":"BooblikClient","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","booblik-client"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient"},"3217":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-0","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"3218":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-1","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#booblikclient","content":"BooblikClient"},"3219":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-2","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#booblikconnection","content":"BooblikConnection"},"3220":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-3","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#the-pending-queue-and-fifo-ordering","content":"The Pending Queue and FIFO Ordering"},"3221":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-4","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#fetch-wait-semantics","content":"Fetch Wait Semantics"},"3222":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-5","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#connectionclosedexception-and-failure-propagation","content":"ConnectionClosedException and Failure Propagation"},"3223":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-6","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#zero-copy-transfer-via-transferto","content":"Zero-Copy Transfer via transferTo"},"3224":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-7","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#key-files","content":"Key files"},"3225":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-8","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#behaviour-that-surprise","content":"Behaviour that surprise"},"3226":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-9","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `f508a4b65b3f`, 2026-08-15, sources: 6. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"3227":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-10","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#booblikclient","content":"The low-level, blocking, single-socket client interface.\n`BooblikClient` provides a raw, blocking interface to the broker, where sending and receiving are separate calls to allow for manual pipelining `BooblikClient.kt:18-22`. It manages a single `SocketChannel` and uses a `nextCorrelationId` to tag requests `BooblikClient.kt:37`."},"3228":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-11","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#booblikconnection","content":"Pipelined request management and correlation ID matching.\n`BooblikConnection` manages a pipelined connection where multiple requests can be in flight simultaneously `BooblikConnection.kt:31`. It uses an `AtomicInteger` to ensure that every caller receives a unique correlation ID, preventing the same ID from being handed to two different callers `BooblikConnection.kt:71`."},"3229":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-12","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#the-pending-queue-and-fifo-ordering","content":"How the client ensures broker response order matches request order via the Pending sealed class.\nTo maintain the protocol's ordering guarantee, the client uses a `ConcurrentLinkedQueue` of `Pending` objects `BooblikConnection.kt:60`. The `Pending` sealed class hierarchy (including `Produce`, `Metadata`, and `Fetch`) implements `checkOrder` to verify that the broker's response correlation ID matches the expected ID, failing loudly if the broker reorders responses `BooblikConnection.kt:192-195`."},"3230":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-13","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#fetch-wait-semantics","content":"Behavior of maxWaitMillis and the impact of held requests on connection pipelining.\nWhen a `fetch` request is sent with a `maxWaitMillis` greater than zero, the broker may hold the request until more data is available or the timeout expires `LongFetchTest.kt:58`. Because the broker serves requests in order, a held fetch blocks all subsequent requests on that same connection, including `PRODUCE` requests `BooblikConnection.kt:132-136`."},"3231":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-14","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#connectionclosedexception-and-failure-propagation","content":"How the client handles socket closures and propagates errors to waiting callers.\nIf a connection fails, the `fail` function iterates through all remaining `Pending` objects in the queue and completes them with a `ConnectionClosedException` `BooblikConnection.kt:166-167`. This ensures that callers waiting on `await()` are not left hanging indefinitely when the socket closes `BooblikConnection.kt:166`."},"3232":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-15","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#zero-copy-transfer-via-transferto","content":"The requirement for SocketChannel to enable sendfile and the risks of wrapping the channel.\nThe `transferFrom` method relies on `FileChannel.transferTo` to achieve zero-copy via `sendfile` `Connection.kt:48`. However, the `transferTarget` must be a real `SocketChannel`; wrapping the channel in a decorator can silently turn the read path into a standard heap-buffer copy loop `SendfileTest.kt:73-76`."},"3233":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-16","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#key-files","content":"File"},"3234":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-17","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#key-files","content":"Lines"},"3235":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-18","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#key-files","content":"What is there"},"3236":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-19","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#key-files","content":"`…/client/BooblikClient.kt`"},"3237":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-20","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#key-files","content":"`24-49`"},"3238":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-21","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#key-files","content":"The `BooblikClient` class providing blocking send/receive methods."},"3239":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-22","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#key-files","content":"`…/client/BooblikConnection.kt`"},"3240":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-23","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#key-files","content":"`50-97`"},"3241":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-24","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#key-files","content":"The `BooblikConnection` class managing the reader and writer coroutines."},"3242":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-25","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#key-files","content":"`…/nio/Connection.kt`"},"3243":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-26","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#key-files","content":"`23-53`"},"3244":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-27","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#key-files","content":"The `Connection` interface defining `transferFrom` and `transferTarget`."},"3245":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-28","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#behaviour-that-surprise","content":"A held `fetch` request on a `BooblikConnection` blocks all subsequent requests on that same connection, meaning a consumer and a producer cannot share a connection if the consumer is waiting for data `BooblikConnection.kt:132-136`."},"3246":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient-29","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/booblikclient#behaviour-that-surprise","content":"Wrapping a `SocketChannel` in a decorator (like a metrics or TLS layer) can silently disable `sendfile` optimizations, causing `transferTo` to fall back to a heap-buffer copy loop without changing the resulting data `SendfileTest.kt:39-41`."},"3247":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","type":"page","content":"booblik-client","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","booblik-client"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client"},"3248":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-0","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"3249":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-1","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client#booblikclient","content":"BooblikClient"},"3250":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-2","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client#booblikconnection","content":"BooblikConnection"},"3251":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-3","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client#producer","content":"Producer"},"3252":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-4","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client#consumer","content":"Consumer"},"3253":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-5","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client#key-files","content":"Key files"},"3254":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-6","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client#public-api","content":"Public API"},"3255":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-7","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"Behaviour that surprises"},"3256":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-8","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `f508a4b65b3f`, 2026-08-15, sources: 6. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"3257":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-9","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#booblikclient","content":"Low-level blocking client for direct socket communication. It provides the foundation for all network activity by managing a single `SocketChannel` and performing raw reads and writes of request frames `BooblikClient.kt:27-88`."},"3258":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-10","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#booblikclient","content":"More: BooblikClient"},"3259":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-11","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#booblikconnection","content":"Pipelined connection with asynchronous request-response matching. This class manages a single socket where multiple requests can be in flight simultaneously; it uses a `ConcurrentLinkedQueue` of `Pending` objects to match incoming responses to their original callers via correlation IDs `BooblikConnection.kt:60-241`."},"3260":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-12","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#producer","content":"Record accumulation and batching mechanism. The `Producer` uses an internal `mailbox` to collect records and groups them into `Batch` objects to maximize throughput, as batching is identified as the most significant performance factor `Producer.kt:37-173`."},"3261":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-13","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#producer","content":"More: Producer"},"3262":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-14","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#consumer","content":"Partition reading and position management. The `Consumer` tracks the `position` (offset) locally rather than relying on the broker to maintain state `Consumer.kt:56-65`, allowing for efficient, zero-copy-friendly reading of partition data `Consumer.kt:56-97`."},"3263":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-15","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#key-files","content":"File"},"3264":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-16","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#key-files","content":"Lines"},"3265":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-17","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#key-files","content":"What is there"},"3266":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-18","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#key-files","content":"`…/client/BooblikClient.kt`"},"3267":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-19","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#key-files","content":"`24-88`"},"3268":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-20","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#key-files","content":"The low-level blocking socket client."},"3269":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-21","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#key-files","content":"`…/client/BooblikConnection.kt`"},"3270":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-22","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#key-files","content":"`50-241`"},"3271":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-23","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wi