"url":"/wiki/booblik-client#public-api","content":"`Producer.kt:21`"},"3295":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-47","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#public-api","content":"Configuration for batching and acknowledgment."},"3296":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-48","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#public-api","content":"`Producer`"},"3297":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-49","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#public-api","content":"`Producer.kt:54`"},"3298":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-50","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#public-api","content":"High-level API for sending batched records."},"3299":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-51","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#public-api","content":"`FetchFailedException`"},"3300":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-52","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#public-api","content":"`Consumer.kt:8`"},"3301":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-53","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#public-api","content":"Thrown when a fetch request fails."},"3302":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-54","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#public-api","content":"`RecordExceedsMaxBytesException`"},"3303":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-55","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#public-api","content":"`Consumer.kt:28`"},"3304":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-56","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#public-api","content":"Thrown when a record is too large to fit in `maxBytes`."},"3305":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-57","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#public-api","content":"`Records`"},"3306":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-58","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#public-api","content":"`Consumer.kt:38`"},"3307":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-59","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#public-api","content":"Data class containing a batch of fetched records."},"3308":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-60","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#public-api","content":"`Consumer`"},"3309":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-61","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#public-api","content":"`Consumer.kt:56`"},"3310":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-62","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#public-api","content":"High-level API for reading partition data."},"3311":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-63","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"In `Producer.runLoop`, the use of `select` with `onTimeout` is critical; using `withTimeoutOrNull` would cancel the `mailbox.receive()` operation, potentially causing the client to drop records and leaving callers waiting forever `Producer.kt:143-158`."},"3312":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-64","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"The `Consumer.poll` method can throw a `RecordExceedsMaxBytesException` if a record is larger than the configured `maxBytes`, which results in a permanent stall if the caller does not increase the limit `Consumer.kt:28-35`."},"3313":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client-65","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"`BooblikConnection` enforces strict FIFO ordering; if the broker responds out of order, the `checkOrder` function will trigger a failure to prevent delivering the wrong response to a caller `BooblikConnection.kt:192-194`."},"3314":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","type":"page","content":"Producer","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","booblik-client"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer"},"3315":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-0","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"What this module is responsible for"},"3316":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-1","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"3317":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-2","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#the-accumulator","content":"The Accumulator"},"3318":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-3","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#command-loop-and-select-semantics","content":"Command Loop and `select` semantics"},"3319":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-4","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#batch-delivery-and-ackpolicy","content":"Batch Delivery and `AckPolicy`"},"3320":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-5","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#drainpending-and-connection-failure","content":"`drainPending` and Connection Failure"},"3321":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-6","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#race-conditions-in-multi-topic-streams","content":"Race conditions in multi-topic streams"},"3322":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-7","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#key-files","content":"Key files"},"3323":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-8","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#behaviour-that-surprising","content":"Behaviour that surprising"},"3324":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-9","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `f508a4b65b3f`, 2026-08-15, sources: 6. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"3325":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-10","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"The `Producer` is responsible for accumulating individual records into batches organized by topic and partition to maximize throughput. Instead of sending every record immediately, it waits until either a maximum batch size is reached or a time limit (`lingerMillis`) expires, significantly reducing the overhead of network round-trips and broker writes (`Producer.kt:23-34`)."},"3326":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-11","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#the-accumulator","content":"The core of the producer is the accumulation logic that groups records by a `Key` (topic and partition) as seen in `Producer.kt:235-238`. The `ProducerConfig` determines how these batches behave:"},"3327":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-12","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#the-accumulator","content":"Parameter"},"3328":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-13","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#the-accumulator","content":"Type"},"3329":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-14","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#the-accumulator","content":"Description"},"3330":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-15","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#the-accumulator","content":"`maxBatchSize`"},"3331":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-16","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#the-accumulator","content":"`Int`"},"3332":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-17","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#the-accumulator","content":"Reached first, the batch goes immediately."},"3333":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-18","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#the-accumulator","content":"`lingerMillis`"},"3334":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-19","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#the-accumulator","content":"`Long`"},"3335":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-20","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#the-accumulator","content":"How long an incomplete batch waits for company."},"3336":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-21","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#the-accumulator","content":"`ackPolicy`"},"3337":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-22","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#the-accumulator","content":"`AckPolicy`"},"3338":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-23","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#the-accumulator","content":"Determines when the caller is notified of success."},"3339":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-24","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#the-accumulator","content":"The timing logic is specifically designed so that the `lingerMillis` window starts from the arrival of the *first* record in a batch, not the last, to prevent a steady trickle of records from postponing a send indefinitely (`Producer.kt:47-49`)."},"3340":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-25","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#command-loop-and-select-semantics","content":"The `runLoop` function manages the lifecycle of incoming commands using a `select` expression to multiplex between receiving new commands from the `mailbox` and waiting for the `lingerMillis` timeout (`Producer.kt:154-158`)."},"3341":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-26","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#command-loop-and-select-semantics","content":"A critical implementation detail is the use of `select` with `onReceiveCatching` rather than `withTimeoutOrNull(mailbox.receive())`. This is because a cancelled `receive` can swallow an element from the channel without delivering it to the logic, causing the caller's `CompletableDeferred` to hang forever (`Producer.kt:143-146`)."},"3342":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-27","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#batch-delivery-and-ackpolicy","content":"When a batch is ready, `deliver` is called to transmit the records via the connection (`Producer.kt:195-200`). The handling of the response depends on the `AckPolicy`:"},"3343":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-28","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#batch-delivery-and-ackpolicy","content":"If the result is `null` (used for `AckPolicy.NONE`), the producer completes all handles with `Offset.ZERO` to indicate the batch was sent, even though no broker acknowledgement was received (`Producer.kt:201-206`)."},"3344":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-29","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#batch-delivery-and-ackpolicy","content":"If an `ErrorCode` is returned, the producer completes the handles with a `ProduceFailedException` (`Producer.kt:208-211`)."},"3345":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-30","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#batch-delivery-and-ackpolicy","content":"On success, it calculates consecutive offsets for the batch (`Producer.kt:214-216`)."},"3346":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-31","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#drainpending-and-connection-failure","content":"If the producer is closed or the connection fails, the `drainPending` function is invoked to ensure no callers are left hanging (`Producer.kt:222-224`). It iterates through all currently pending batches and completes their `CompletableDeferred` handles with a `ConnectionClosedException` (`Producer.kt:223`). It then drains any remaining commands in the `mailbox` to ensure the coroutine terminates cleanly (`Producer.kt:227-232`)."},"3347":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-32","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#race-conditions-in-multi-topic-streams","content":"A specific edge case exists when a single `Producer` handles multiple topics at different arrival rates. If a record arrives exactly when the `lingerMillis` timer expires, a race condition in the `runLoop` can cause a `receive` operation to be cancelled, swallowing a record and causing a hang (`Producer.kt:154-158`). This is verified by tests that drive two topics at different rates to force the collision (`ProducerLostRecordTest.kt:52-53`)."},"3348":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-33","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#key-files","content":"File"},"3349":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-34","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#key-files","content":"Lines"},"3350":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-35","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#key-files","content":"What is there"},"3351":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-36","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#key-files","content":"`…/client/Producer.kt`"},"3352":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-37","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#key-files","content":"`21-34`"},"3353":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-38","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#key-files","content":"`ProducerConfig` definition and batching parameters."},"3354":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-39","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#key-files","content":"`…/client/Producer.kt`"},"3355":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-40","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#key-files","content":"`54-86`"},"3356":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-41","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#key-files","content":"`Producer` class definition and `send` method."},"3357":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-42","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#key-files","content":"`…/client/Producer.kt`"},"3358":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-43","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#key-files","content":"`123-173`"},"3359":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-44","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#key-files","content":"The `runLoop` implementation and `select` logic."},"3360":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-45","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#key-files","content":"`…/client/Producer.kt`"},"3361":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-46","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#key-files","content":"`195-220`"},"3362":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-47","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#key-files","content":"The `deliver` method and acknowledgement handling."},"3363":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-48","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#key-files","content":"`…/net/ProducerLostRecordTest.kt`"},"3364":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-49","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#key-files","content":"`41-53`"},"3365":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-50","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#key-files","content":"Test case for multi-topic rate collisions."},"3366":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-51","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#behaviour-that-surprising","content":"The `send` function in `Producer` does not actually send the record to the wire immediately; it merely queues it in a `mailbox`, meaning the returned `CompletableDeferred` only completes once the batch is actually delivered (`Producer.kt:75-76`)."},"3367":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-52","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#behaviour-that-surprising","content":"In `runLoop`, the `lingerMillis` timer is calculated based on the first record of a batch, which prevents a \"steady trickle\" of records from indefinitely postponing a send (`Producer.kt:47-49`)."},"3368":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer-53","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-client/producer#behaviour-that-surprising","content":"The `deliver` method uses `batch.answers.forEachIndexed` to assign consecutive offsets to records in a batch, assuming the broker assigns them sequentially (`Producer.kt:214-216`)."},"3369":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","type":"page","content":"booblik-core","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","booblik-core"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core"},"3370":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-0","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"3371":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-1","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core#logsegment","content":"LogSegment"},"3372":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-2","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core#segmentmode","content":"SegmentMode"},"3373":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-3","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core#partitionlog","content":"PartitionLog"},"3374":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-4","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core#recovery-after-a-crash","content":"Recovery after a crash"},"3375":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-5","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core#the-write-actor-and-group-commit","content":"The write actor and group commit"},"3376":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-6","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core#fetchslice-and-zero-copy-reading","content":"FetchSlice and zero-copy reading"},"3377":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-7","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core#key-files","content":"Key files"},"3378":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-8","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core#public-api","content":"Public API"},"3379":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-9","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/booblik-core#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"Behaviour that surprises"},"3380":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-10","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `f508a4b65b3f`, 2026-08-15, sources: 6. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"3381":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-11","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core#logsegment","content":"The physical storage unit consisting of an append-only data file and a sparse index. It manages the actual byte-level operations, including appending records with headers and performing position lookups via a `SparseOffsetIndex` (`LogSegment.kt:41-47`)."},"3382":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-12","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core#segmentmode","content":"Comparison between `FILE_CHANNEL` and `MAPPED` write paths and their implications for the buffer cache:"},"3383":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-13","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core#segmentmode","content":"Mode"},"3384":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-14","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core#segmentmode","content":"Description"},"3385":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-15","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core#segmentmode","content":"`FILE_CHANNEL`"},"3386":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-16","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core#segmentmode","content":"Uses a plain `FileChannel` for writes; the file length is the end of the log (`LogSegment.kt:25`)."},"3387":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-17","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core#segmentmode","content":"`MAPPED`"},"3388":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-18","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core#segmentmode","content":"Uses a memory-mapped file; the segment is pre-sized to its full capacity, and the end is marked by a zero length prefix (`LogSegment.kt:25-289`)."},"3389":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-19","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core#partitionlog","content":"Management of multiple segments, segment rolling, and the retention mechanism. It maintains an immutable list of segments that is replaced on every change to ensure thread-safe visibility without locks (`PartitionLog.kt:18-23`)."},"3390":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-20","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core#recovery-after-a-crash","content":"The process of rebuilding the `SparseOffsetIndex` by walking record headers and verifying checksums. During recovery, the system scans the file in large chunks to find record boundaries and discards any trailing partial records or corrupted data (`LogSegment.kt:321-373`)."},"3391":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-21","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core#recovery-after-a-crash","content":"More: Recovery after a crash"},"3392":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-22","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core#the-write-actor-and-group-commit","content":"The `PartitionWriter` coroutine, mailbox processing, and the mechanics of batching and flushing. It uses a single coroutine to own the write side of a partition, draining the mailbox to group multiple `WriteCommand`s into a single batch to amortize the cost of disk barriers (`PartitionWriter.kt:163-197`)."},"3393":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-23","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core#fetchslice-and-zero-copy-reading","content":"The lifecycle of a `FetchSlice` and how `transferTo` enables high-throughput streaming without heap overhead. A `FetchSlice` acts as a held claim on a contiguous run of bytes, ensuring that a segment is not retired while a `transferTo` operation is streaming data to a `WritableByteChannel` (`PartitionLog.kt:132-145`)."},"3394":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-24","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core#key-files","content":"File"},"3395":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-25","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core#key-files","content":"Lines"},"3396":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-26","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core#key-files","content":"What is there"},"3397":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-27","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core#key-files","content":"`…/storage/LogSegment.kt`"},"3398":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-28","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core#key-files","content":"`41-48`"},"3399":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-29","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core#key-files","content":"The `LogSegment` class which manages a single data file and its index."},"3400":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-30","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core#key-files","content":"`…/storage/Log.kt`"},"3401":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-31","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/booblik-core#key-files","content":"`17-47`"},"3402":{"id":"/wiki/booblik-core-32","page_id":"/wiki/booblik-core","tags":[],