l":"/wiki/dev-relay#directional-modes","content":"`KAFKA_TO_BOOBLIK`"},"4631":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-15","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#directional-modes","content":"Moves data from Kafka to booblik"},"4632":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-16","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#directional-modes","content":"Managed by Kafka via Consumer Groups (`Directions.kt:46`)"},"4633":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-17","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#directional-modes","content":"`BOOBLIK_TO_KAFKA`"},"4634":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-18","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#directional-modes","content":"Moves data from booblik to Kafka"},"4635":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-19","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#directional-modes","content":"Managed locally via `FileOffsetStore` (`Directions.kt:93`)"},"4636":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-20","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#directional-modes","content":"More: Directional modes"},"4637":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-21","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#boobliktokafka","content":"This mode consumes data from booblik and produces it to Kafka. Because the booblik broker does not remember reader positions, the relay uses a `FileOffsetStore` to manage state locally on the relay's volume (`Directions.kt:93`). To ensure at-least-once delivery, the producer is configured with `acks=all` (`Directions.kt:102`)."},"4638":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-22","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#boobliktokafka","content":"More: booblikToKafka"},"4639":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-23","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#at-least-once-delivery-guarantees","content":"The relay implements at-least-once delivery by ensuring the position is only updated after the destination has acknowledged the data. In `kafkaToBooblik`, `consumer.commitSync()` is called only after all records in a batch are sent to booblik (`Directions.kt:71`). In `booblikToKafka`, the `checkpointing` mechanism saves the position only after the `kafka.flush()` operation is complete (`Directions.kt:119`)."},"4640":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-24","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#relaystats","content":"The monitoring surface is exposed via an HTTP server and provides real-time metrics through the `Stats` class (`Main.kt:88`). The `RelayStats` data class (`Main.kt:129`) includes:"},"4641":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-25","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#relaystats","content":"`relayed`: Total count of relayed records."},"4642":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-26","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#relaystats","content":"`batches`: Total number of batches processed."},"4643":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-27","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#relaystats","content":"`position`: The last observed offset/position."},"4644":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-28","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#relaystats","content":"`restarts`: Number of times the relay loop has restarted due to failures."},"4645":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-29","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#relaystats","content":"`lastFailure`: The message of the last encountered exception."},"4646":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-30","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#relaystats","content":"`lastRecord`: A 120-character sample of the last record."},"4647":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-31","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#relayconfig","content":"The relay is configured via environment variables as defined in `Main.kt:142-176`. 