lay#key-files","content":"`142-176`"},"4701":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-85","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#key-files","content":"The `RelayConfig` data class and environment loading logic."},"4702":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-86","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#behaviour-that-surprise","content":"The `kafkaToBooblik` function uses `consumer.commitSync()` (`Directions.kt:71`) to ensure that a crash between sending data and committing the offset results in a repeated batch rather than data loss."},"4703":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-87","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#behaviour-that-surprise","content":"The `booblikToKafka` function requires an explicit `kafka.flush()` (`Directions.kt:119`) before the `checkpointing` mechanism updates the local `FileOffsetStore` to maintain delivery guarantees."},"4704":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-88","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#behaviour-that-surprise","content":"The `main` function (`Main.kt:47`) uses a `while(true)` loop with a `try-catch` block to ensure that the relay automatically restarts if a connection to either Kafka or booblik is lost."},"4705":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay-89","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay#more","content":"kafkaToBooblik"},"4706":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","type":"page","content":"kafkaToBooblik","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki","dev/relay"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik"},"4707":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-0","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"What this module is responsible for"},"4708":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-1","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"4709":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-2","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#kafkaconsumer-configuration-and-properties","content":"KafkaConsumer configuration and properties"},"4710":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-3","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#the-at-least-once-delivery-guarantee","content":"The at-least-once delivery guarantee"},"4711":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-4","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#per-key-ordering-preservation","content":"Per-key ordering preservation"},"4712":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-5","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#the-relay-restart-loop-and-error-handling","content":"The relay restart loop and error handling"},"4713":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-6","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#relay-statistics-and-observability","content":"Relay statistics and observability"},"4714":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-7","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#key-files","content":"Key files"},"4715":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-8","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"Behaviour that surprises"},"4716":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-9","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","content":"Model `gemma-mtp`, commit `f508a4b65b3f`, 2026-08-15, sources: 6. Edit the code or the hand-written documentation instead."},"4717":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-10","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#what-this-module-is-responsible-for","content":"The `kafkaToBooblik` function acts as a bridge that translates data from a Kafka topic into the booblik format. It consumes batches of records from Kafka and pushes them into a booblik topic, ensuring that the data is safely acknowledged by the booblik broker before the Kafka consumer advances its position."},"4718":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-11","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#kafkaconsumer-configuration-and-properties","content":"The Kafka consumer is configured to ensure manual control over the message lifecycle. It uses `ByteArrayDeserializer` for both keys and values to treat all data as raw bytes `Directions.kt:47-48`. Crucially, `ENABLE_AUTO_COMMIT_CONFIG` is set to `false` to prevent the consumer from automatically advancing offsets before the data is safely stored in booblik `Directions.kt:49`. The `AUTO_OFFSET_RESET_CONFIG` is set to `earliest` to ensure that a new relay can catch up on all existing data in the topic `Directions.kt:51`."},"4719":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-12","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#the-at-least-once-delivery-guarantee","content":"The relay implements an at-least-once delivery guarantee through a strict sequence of operations in the polling loop. First, it maps the records to `handle.send` calls, which are asynchronous `acknowledgements` `Directions.kt:66`. It then calls `await()` on these acknowledgements to ensure every record in the batch has been processed by the booblik broker `Directions.kt:67`. Only after all records are acknowledged does it call `consumer.commitSync()` `Directions.kt:71`. This order ensures that if a crash occurs between sending and committing, the batch will be re-delivered upon restart `Directions.kt:70`."},"4720":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-13","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#per-key-ordering-preservation","content":"Even though the booblik wire protocol does not store Kafka keys `research-usecases.md:37-41`, the relay preserves per-key ordering during the crossing. When `handle.send(record.value(), key = record.key())` is called, the Kafka key is used to determine the target booblik partition `Directions.kt:66`. Because the key determines the partition, all records with the same key are routed to the same booblik partition, maintaining their relative order `Directions.kt:34-35`."},"4721":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-14","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#the-relay-restart-loop-and-error-handling","content":"The relay is designed to be resilient against transient failures on either side of the connection. The main loop is wrapped in a `while (true)` block within a `CoroutineScope` initialized with a `SupervisorJob` `Main.kt:54-55`. If an exception occurs, the error is caught, logged, and the loop restarts after a 2-second delay `Main.kt:61-68`. This prevents the relay from dying permanently if one side (Kafka or booblik) experiences a temporary outage `Main.kt:62-63`."},"4722":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-15","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#relay-statistics-and-observability","content":"Observability is provided through the `Stats` class, which tracks the progress of the relay. The `observe` function updates several metrics whenever a batch is processed `Main.kt:102-111`."},"4723":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-16","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#relay-statistics-and-observability","content":"Metric"},"4724":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-17","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#relay-statistics-and-observability","content":"Description"},"4725":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-18","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#relay-statistics-and-observability","content":"`relayed`"},"4726":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-19","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#relay-statistics-and-observability","content":"Total number of records processed"},"4727":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-20","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#relay-statistics-and-observability","content":"`batches`"},"4728":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-21","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#relay-statistics-and-observability","content":"Total number of batches processed"},"4729":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-22","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#relay-statistics-and-observability","content":"`restarts`"},"4730":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-23","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#relay-statistics-and-observability","content":"Total number of times the relay loop has restarted"},"4731":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-24","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#relay-statistics-and-observability","content":"`position`"},"4732":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-25","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#relay-statistics-and-observability","content":"The last processed offset/value"},"4733":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-26","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#relay-statistics-and-observability","content":"`lastRecord`"},"4734":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-27","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#relay-statistics-and-observability","content":"A string sample (up to 120 chars) of the last record"},"4735":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-28","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#relay-statistics-and-observability","content":"The `RelayStats` data class provides a serializable snapshot of these metrics for the HTTP `/stats` endpoint `Main.kt:129-140`."},"4736":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-29","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#key-files","content":"File"},"4737":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-30","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#key-files","content":"Lines"},"4738":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-31","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#key-files","content":"What is there"},"4739":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-32","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#key-files","content":"`…/relay/Directions.kt`"},"4740":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-33","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#key-files","content":"`38-77`"},"4741":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-34","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#key-files","content":"Implementation of the `kafkaToBooblik` function and its logic."},"4742":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-35","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#key-files","content":"`…/relay/Main.kt`"},"4743":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-36","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#key-files","content":"`47-81`"},"4744":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-37","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#key-files","content":"The `main` function, the `Stats` class, and the `RelayStats` data class."},"4745":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-38","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"**Key Loss**: While `handle.send` uses the key to maintain partition ordering, the key itself is not stored in booblik, meaning it cannot be recovered when reading from booblik back to Kafka `research-usecases.md:37-41`."},"4746":{"id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik-39","page_id":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/wiki/dev-relay/kafkatobooblik#behaviour-that-surprises","content":"**At-least-once Duplicates**: Because `consumer.commitSync()` happens after the booblik write, a crash between these two steps results in the same records being sent again upon restart, making duplicates a legal and expected behavior `Directions.kt:70-72`."},"4747":{"id":"/wiki/github/benchmark-execution-and","page_id":"/wiki/github/benchmark-execution-and","type":"page","content":"Benchmark execution and reporting","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Wiki",".github"],"tags":[],"url":"/wiki/github/benchmark-execution-and"},"4748":{"id":"/wiki/github/benchmark-execution-and-0","page_id":"/wiki/github/benchmark-execution-and","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/wiki/github/benchmark-execution-and#diagram","content":"Diagram"},"4749":{"id":"/wiki/github/ben