op"],[4634,"Moves data from booblik to Kafka"],[4631,"Moves data from Kafka to booblik"],[4013,"Name of the consumer instance"],[3624,"NIO-based selector loop"],[3843,"Non-blocking NIO with a dedicated selector thread and coroutine suspension."],[3055,"Number of records before a flush"],[4722,"Observability is provided through the `Stats` class, which tracks the progress of the relay. The `observe` function updates several metrics whenever a batch is processed `Main.kt:102-111`."],[3345,"On success, it calculates consecutive offsets for the batch (`Producer.kt:214-216`)."],[4311,"Once a connection is successfully established, `openConnection` returns a new `BooblikConnection` instance (`Main.kt:80`). Crucially, this connection is initialized with its own `CoroutineScope` configured with a `SupervisorJob` (`Main.kt:80`). This ensures that failures in child coroutines within the connection do not automatically cancel the entire scope, allowing for more robust error handling during the publisher's execution."],[4413,"Once a task is marked as `DONE`, it cannot be claimed again (`ClaimStateTest.kt:63-69`)."],[4805,"Once the image is verified, the workflow performs a dual-push to GHCR. It tags the specific versioned image (e.g., `:0.1.0`) and the `:latest` pointer `release.yml:87-89`. This ensures that users can always pull the most recent stable version via the `:latest` tag while maintaining a permanent record of specific releases `release.yml:88`."],[61,"one actor per partition, group commit, three ack policies (`NONE`, `WRITTEN`, `FORCED`)"],[4243,"openConnection"],[4299,"openConnection"],[3643,"Option"],[44,"Or build it yourself — the script runs the gate, then `installDist`, then `docker build`, in that\norder, because the image has no build stage and a bare `docker build .` would package whatever\nhappens to be sitting in `booblik-app/build/install`:"],[4949,"Orchestration of the split assertion check."],[2,"Overview"],[3736,"Own selector loop, one coroutine per co